    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **70 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner read model so that `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `riskFlag` boolean (read-only) property to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator produces `getRiskFlag`/`setRiskFlag` on the generated `OwnerDto` and MapStruct wires it up automatically (same pattern as the existing derived fields).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the derived logic:\n   - `getRiskFlag()` returns `true` when **any** of the three conditions hold:\n     - the owner is a possible duplicate (`possibleDuplicate` set at create time),\n     - the email domain is **disposable-adjacent**, or\n     - the city is over its soft capacity (`capacityWarning`, i.e. the city held \u226540 owners at creation);\n     otherwise `false`.\n   - `isDisposableAdjacentEmail()` flags emails whose domain shares a known disposable provider's base label (e.g. `mailinator`) via a subdomain (`x.mailinator.com`) or a different TLD (`mailinator.net`) \u2014 cases the exact-match create-time blocklist deliberately doesn't reject. A missing/empty email yields `false`.\n\nThe three conditions reuse the existing computed-and-stored fields (`possibleDuplicate`, `capacityWarning`) plus the stored email, so `riskFlag` reflects the state at creation time, consistent with the surrounding rules. The new `Cp58Tests` (normal owner \u2192 `riskFlag` false) passes, as do all other existing tests.",
